Z||000015||Raydar||12-11-2001||09:53 AM||||Wow! Glad I wasn't there!<P>There used to be an event at Road Atlanta called the Walter Mitty Challenge. <BR>Basically, folks got to bring their expensive cars out and flog them. Lots of Porsches and Ferraris. One guy launched his Lotus <I>over</I> the guardrail and into the woods. <BR>This was after he told his wife that he was going to play golf because she didn't want him to go racing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> <BR>Can <I>you</I> say "busted"? <P>Lots of fun though. I was a corner worker. We used to hold up cards and "rate" the spins at turn 11.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
